{"title":"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_22\">Problem 22</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 22\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A Katende number is a four-digit positive integer where the first two digits and the last two digits, in order, form two integers that are increasing consecutive multiples of some positive integer. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is a Katende number because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac4dbe1c696d11e8dc43dd7f613199b2120daa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\times$\" width=\"11\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac4dbe1c696d11e8dc43dd7f613199b2120daa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\times$\" width=\"11\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89e11acdf0a62baf95b2e576e91d39aa8ee2c327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2346$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/2915d7684ca03be5368a5ceb6e8da03151075c74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2324$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> are Katende numbers. How many Katende numbers are there that are greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e4208d59c57ee9a549ff172069df39fac811d562.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2400$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> and less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/2/592c1d4eacb3ec769d6ac9542733c10632610d91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2600$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since we are looking for values between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e4208d59c57ee9a549ff172069df39fac811d562.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2400$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/2/592c1d4eacb3ec769d6ac9542733c10632610d91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2600$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />, the first two digits must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Case 1: The first two digits are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> factors for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> Katende numbers to be made with it.\n</p><p>Case 2: The first two digits are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> factors for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> Katende numbers to be made with it.\n</p><p>So, in total, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/5/665844a545f49bddc255ac149c5d93d4042ec5a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd34aa5e4f49c065b66db919bf81d6d611bc2bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" /> Katende numbers satisfying the condition.\n</p><p>~any1sgame and edited slightly by anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley\">2025 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 23 (page does not exist)\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> 